  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "GitHub is the approval surface",
      "items": [
        "Host setup authority creates the selected GitHub Environment and nonsecret approval variable after verifying App installation access.",
        "The installer previews the bound controller/repository/profile. No broker login, browser ceremony or admin page; Codex sign-in remains separate."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Current implementation boundary",
      "items": [
        "Controller validation, caching and renewal exist. An operator-supplied enrollment file is an integration input.",
        "The packaged installer still wires direct PEM mode. No hosted broker is supplied by main."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Approved policy: repository-owned authority",
      "items": [
        "The exact marker and durable active grant authorize renewal; a particular person leaving does not revoke it. Names are user-selectable.",
        "Azure Table Storage is selected. Marker absence/change closes observed enrollment permanently; fresh enrollment is required. Detailed freshness/recreation/race proof remains a gate. Plan sources: issues #30/#31/#39/#51-54."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Security boundary",
      "items": [
        "The auth service runs no coding agent. Shared App signing authority stays outside user controllers.",
        "Same-UID agent processes can read local device/token credentials; the bound scope limits their authority."
      ]
    }
  ]
